Screen-shader regions run at their paint order.

The batch iterator already yields each region sequence at its place in
the scene, but the renderer skipped those batches and ran every region
in one go at the overlay boundary, over the fully composed main scene.
That read the whole window into any region pass, so a shader recorded
early (a backdrop treatment under the panels) distorted everything
painted after it. Now each region batch splits the main pass where it
stands: compose so far, shade, resume with Load. Later primitives draw
over the shaded result untouched.

